-- title:
--   Supersingular maximal ideals agreeing on q-substituted functions coincide
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$); assume $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Assume further that $k_0$ contains a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity $\xi$ and that some ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField (q^2 * M') H₁`; let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed non-zero. Let $K''$ be the analogous field for level $M'$ with subgroup the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. Put $C =$ `chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$. Let $y_1, y_2$ be maximal ideals of $C$, both containing the image of $\pi_0$, and assume: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y_1$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point; and that $y_1$ and $y_2$ contain the same elements $x$ of $C$ whose Laurent series is obtained from the Laurent series of some $g \in K''$ by multiplying all exponents by $q$ (the map `qExpand k₀ q`). Then $y_1 = y_2$.
--
--   This is a separation statement for closed points of the integral chart attached to the modular curve of level $H_1 \subseteq (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ over the henselian base $A_0$: a maximal ideal lying over the maximal ideal of $A_0$ at which the $j$-invariant becomes supersingular is pinned down by the restriction of functions coming, via the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$, from the prime-to-$q$ level $M'$ field. It is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin), within the analysis of the reduction at $q$ of modular curves of level divisible by $q^2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_coe_eq_qExpand_iff_chartAlgFin.lean

